### Custom ignores
# Repo-root CLAUDE.md documents THIS repo. Stowing it put a copy at ~/CLAUDE.md,
# and since $HOME is an ancestor of every project, Claude Code loaded the whole
# dotfiles guide (Homebrew, stow, Brewfile, zsh, Raycast, JDKs) into every session
# in every project: ~1700 tokens of irrelevant context everywhere. Unstowed
# 25.07.2026 so it applies only when working inside ~/dotfiles.
# The intentionally-global instructions live in .claude/CLAUDE.md, which stows to
# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. Do not confuse the two.
#
# BOTH patterns must stay anchored with ^/ . A pattern containing no "/" is
# compiled by stow into a *segment* regexp and tested against every path
# component (Stow.pm::ignore), so a bare `CLAUDE.md` here also matched
# .claude/CLAUDE.md and silently refused to stow the global instructions: on a
# machine where ~/.claude already exists as a real dir, stow linked RTK.md,
# commands, rules and settings.json but skipped the one file that @-imports
# RTK.md. Anchored 28.07.2026. AGENTS.md is a symlink to CLAUDE.md and was
# reinstating the identical ~/AGENTS.md leak for every agent that reads it.
^/CLAUDE\.md$
^/AGENTS\.md$
fonts
vscode
macos
scripts
Brewfile
install.sh
browser/*
images/*
google-cloud-sdk
\.config/op
\.claude/skills
\.claude/plugins/known_marketplaces.json
\.agents
\.agent
\.cursor
\.kiro
\.windsurf

### NOTE: stow has no negation syntax. The three `!`-prefixed lines that used to
### sit here looked like an allowlist for Library/Application Support/Code/User,
### but stow compiled them as ordinary regexps that match nothing, so they
### excluded nothing and granted nothing. All of Library/ is stowed, which is the
### actual behaviour and is what CLAUDE.md now documents. Removed 28.07.2026.

### Default ignores

# Comments and blank lines are allowed
RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules

\.DS_Store   # Finder metadata; never symlink into $HOME
.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
